@startuml sequence-diagram-example
' =============================================================
' CEN206 - Week 5: PlantUML Sequence Diagram Example
' Login flow with alt, loop, and opt fragments.
' =============================================================

title CEN206 - Login Sequence Diagram

actor User
participant "LoginPage\n<<UI>>" as UI
participant "AuthService\n<<Service>>" as Auth
participant "UserRepository\n<<Repository>>" as Repo
database "Database" as DB

== Initialization ==

User -> UI : open login page
activate UI
UI --> User : display login form
deactivate UI

== Login Attempt ==

User -> UI : enter credentials\n(username, password)
activate UI

UI -> Auth : authenticate(username, password)
activate Auth

Auth -> Repo : findByUsername(username)
activate Repo

Repo -> DB : SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE username = ?
activate DB
DB --> Repo : ResultSet
deactivate DB

Repo --> Auth : User object (or null)
deactivate Repo

' --- Alt fragment: user found vs. not found ---
alt User found

    Auth -> Auth : verifyPassword(password, hash)

    alt Password correct

        Auth -> Repo : updateLastLogin(userId)
        activate Repo
        Repo -> DB : UPDATE users SET\nlast_login = NOW()
        activate DB
        DB --> Repo : OK
        deactivate DB
        Repo --> Auth : success
        deactivate Repo

        Auth --> UI : AuthResult(SUCCESS, token)

        UI --> User : redirect to dashboard

    else Password incorrect

        Auth -> Auth : incrementFailedAttempts()

        ' --- Opt fragment: lock account ---
        opt failedAttempts >= 3

            Auth -> Repo : lockAccount(userId)
            activate Repo
            Repo -> DB : UPDATE users SET\nlocked = true
            activate DB
            DB --> Repo : OK
            deactivate DB
            Repo --> Auth : account locked
            deactivate Repo

            Auth --> UI : AuthResult(LOCKED)
            UI --> User : "Account locked.\nContact admin."

        end

        Auth --> UI : AuthResult(INVALID_PASSWORD)
        UI --> User : "Invalid password.\nPlease try again."

    end

else User not found

    Auth --> UI : AuthResult(USER_NOT_FOUND)
    deactivate Auth

    UI --> User : "User not found.\nPlease register."
    deactivate UI

end

== Retry Loop ==

loop up to 3 times (while not authenticated)

    User -> UI : re-enter credentials
    activate UI

    UI -> Auth : authenticate(username, password)
    activate Auth
    Auth --> UI : AuthResult
    deactivate Auth

    UI --> User : result
    deactivate UI

end

note over User, DB
  This diagram demonstrates:
  - alt/else (conditional branching)
  - opt (optional fragment)
  - loop (repeated interaction)
  - activation bars (object lifelines)
end note

@enduml
